{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T2-001", "approach": "B1", "approach_base": "B1", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "Order, listed as number 3 in his plan, with the precept: \"Let all your things have their places; let each part of your business have its time.\"\n\nFranklin found it hardest because:\n- A journeyman printer could manage his own time, but a master must mix with the world and receive people of business at their own hours, so exact observance was impossible.\n- As to places for things and papers, he found it extremely difficult to acquire, having not been early accustomed to it.\n- His exceedingly good memory made him less sensible of the inconvenience of want of method.\n- He made so little progress and had such frequent relapses that he was almost ready to give up the attempt and content himself with a faulty character, like the man who decided he liked a speckled ax best.", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 9 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::o031", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::p1_b376"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 0, "span": [187016, 187025], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 84 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::o031", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::p1_b377"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 1, "span": [187027, 187111], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 2225 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::o031", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-20203_franklin_autobiography.en::p1_b422"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 2, "span": [195322, 197547], "meta": {}}], "evidence_units": ["K.gutenberg-20203_frankli