"openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash", "chat_digest": "openrouter"}, "replicate": 0, "setting": "en-en", "rid": "070db28d08b14a091714", "code_sig": "094d16a548662280", "question_sig": "be3f68e4bc025c9a", "pool_sha1": "aa11d6c898b9bdfa106d9c97b01b47110eceb2c9"}}, "structured": null}
{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T2-002", "approach": "B1", "approach_base": "B1", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "Frederick Douglass first learned from Mrs. Auld, finished learning from white street boys, and Mr. Auld stopped the lessons because teaching a slave to read was unlawful, unsafe, and would make the slave unmanageable.\n\n- Mrs. Auld kindly began teaching him the A, B, C and to spell words of three or four letters (Chapter VI).\n- Mr. Auld found out and forbade her to continue, saying it was unlawful as well as unsafe to teach a slave to read (Chapter VI).\n- He argued that learning would spoil a slave, make him unmanageable, of no value to his master, and discontented and unhappy (Chapter VI).\n- Douglass then adopted the plan of making friends of little white boys he met in the street and converting them into teachers (Chapter VII).\n- He took his book on errands and traded bread to the hungry boys in exchange for lessons, finally succeeding in learning to read (Chapter VII).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 2781 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o011", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b110"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 0, "span": [76533, 79314], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 1698 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o012", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b116"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 1, "span": [84733, 86431], "meta": {}}], "evidence_units": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b110", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b116"], "evidence_items": [{"doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o011", "kind": "unit", "chars": 2781, "unit_ids":